WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.420
It's official: fans are loving&nbsp;
the new "Star Wars" show "Ahsoka",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.298
and they're taking to social media&nbsp;
in droves to share their thoughts.

00:00:06.298 --> 00:00:08.698
Minor spoilers for the first two episodes ahead!

00:00:08.698 --> 00:00:14.400
After the standalone series starring Rosario&nbsp;
Dawson premiered on Disney+ on August 22, 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.760
fans hopped on social media to discuss&nbsp;
just how happy they were with the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.960
which takes place a few years after the events of&nbsp;
the beloved animated series "Star Wars: Rebels."

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.520
Led by "Star Wars" guru Dave Filoni, the&nbsp;
series also stars Natasha Liu Bordizzo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.440
Mary Elizabeth Winstead, Ivanna Sakhno, and the&nbsp;
late Ray Stevenson in one of his final roles.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.318
So what do fans really think of&nbsp;
the latest "Star Wars" project?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:38.121
After seeing Dawson bring the character into&nbsp;
the live-action realm in "The Mandalorian",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:42.429
they're thrilled her solo adventure is off to&nbsp;
such a strong start. One fan posted on Twitter,

00:00:42.429 --> 00:00:45.900
"The first two episodes of ["Ahsoka"] just&nbsp;
deliver on every front. Everything that made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.840
Rebels so special is beautifully&nbsp;
translated into live action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:53.169
and the heart and soul of this incredible story&nbsp;
remains strong. Filoni has done it once again."

00:00:53.169 --> 00:00:56.458
General Syndulla, it's good to see you."
"And you."

00:00:56.458 --> 00:00:58.140
Another fan agreed, posting,

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.960
"First episode of ["Ahsoka"] is&nbsp;
breathtakingly beautiful and I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.600
in tears with how well done they've&nbsp;
brought the animation to real life!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.813 --> 00:01:07.473
A sweet and fitting tribute to Ray&nbsp;
Stevenson and an amazing cliffhanger."

00:01:07.473 --> 00:01:10.000
Another fan kept it simple&nbsp;
with their reaction, posting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.260
"Last night's premiere was EPIC!" Meanwhile,&nbsp;
this fan got much more specific, writing,

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.820
"I think one thing I really loved about the first&nbsp;
2 episodes of ["Ahsoka"] is that the show really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.020
isn't afraid to take its time. Each scene and&nbsp;
moment [feels] appropriately drawn out and we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.380
get to sit with the characters for longer&nbsp;
than any moments in Mando ever allowed."

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.560
"You're gonna want to hear what she has to say."

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.980
Dawson already charmed audiences in&nbsp;
"The Mandalorian," and as a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.373
she's built up a lot of goodwill as the&nbsp;
character — which this fan made clear.

00:01:35.373 --> 00:01:39.060
"I just watched the first 2 episodes of&nbsp;
Ahsoka and holy sh*t how good Rosario&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:42.480
Dawson is leaning into this role [...]&nbsp;
The best piece of media so far this year."

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.480
Another fan made it clear that even&nbsp;
if you're not a "Star Wars" expert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.277
there's something for everyone on this show:

00:01:47.277 --> 00:01:50.820
"I honestly think the first 2 episodes of&nbsp;
["Ahsoka"] do a great job introducing all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.040
the main story beats and characters to prep anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.820
to be able to understand and enjoy it even&nbsp;
if you haven't seen Rebels or Clone Wars."

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:00.240
There's even something for "Star Wars"&nbsp;
fans who have serious franchise fatigue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.740
according to this fan, who posted,

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:05.830
"I actually like it a lot so far and I've been&nbsp;
super critical of Disney canon for the most part."

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:09.480
Translating a beloved animated show into&nbsp;
live-action could have been a tough feat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.740
but clearly, Filoni and his cast met this&nbsp;
challenge head-on. As one excited fan wrote,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.460
"The first two episodes of ["Ahsoka"]&nbsp;
were so freaking good like imo this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.060
is already some of the best Star Wars&nbsp;
content. POETIC CINEMA The Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.300
Rebels solidarity! Man I cannot&nbsp;
wait for more episodes to come."

00:02:24.418 --> 00:02:26.038
Another fan agreed, saying,

00:02:26.038 --> 00:02:30.420
"I didn't want ["Ahsoka"] episode 2 to end. This&nbsp;
felt like live action REBELS, especially with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.640
music. CHOPPER BABY!!! The casting is perfect.&nbsp;
Sabine Wren being Ahsoka's apprentice is epic."

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.323
"Nice hair cut."

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.769
"It's more me." 

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:43.860
Some fans just felt elated seeing their favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.140
characters make the leap from&nbsp;
animation to live-action:

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.680
"I can't explain the serotonin rush I&nbsp;
get watching Ahsoka and seeing Hera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.700
Sabine and Lothal in live-action. So&nbsp;
impressed with how good it is so far."

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.020
Decider writer Meghan O'Keefe posted that fans&nbsp;
of the latest major "Star Wars" project, "Andor",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.480
might take issue with "Ahsoka,"&nbsp;
but she liked it all the same.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.040
"Initial ["Ahsoka"] thoughts: Dave Filoni lovingly&nbsp;
brings his rebels to life in a story that embraces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.720
mythology, magic, and lore in a way that could&nbsp;
turn off, say, ANDOR fans. Slower paced than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:14.877
expected but still enthralling for this Rebels&nbsp;
fan. Natasha Liu Bordizzo is my early MVP."

00:03:14.877 --> 00:03:18.000
Other fans were relieved that Ahsoka,&nbsp;
who wasn't wildly popular at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.520
is finally getting her due,&nbsp;
like this fan, who posted,

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.660
"Well it took 15 years but I've finally seen&nbsp;
the introduction of Ahsoka Tano who went from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.740
a character Star Wars fans initially hated to one&nbsp;
of the most beloved characters in the franchise."

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.980
The bottom line is this: fans&nbsp;
really, really like "Ahsoka."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.400
Even diehard "Star Wars" fans are&nbsp;
on board. YouTuber StarWarsTheory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.190
who's definitely an expert in the field, gave&nbsp;
the series his seal of approval, posting,

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.740
"Just watched Ahsoka again to complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.280
my breakdown of episodes 1 + 2 and I like&nbsp;
it even more the second time around."

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.661
The first two episodes of "Ahsoka"&nbsp;
are streaming on Disney+ now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.661 --> 00:03:49.941
and new episodes drop on&nbsp;
the service every Tuesday.

